1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,280
The dunes in this game sparkle as you move.

2
00:00:03,280 --> 00:00:04,740
Even grains smaller than a pixel

3
00:00:04,740 --> 00:00:08,080
do not all need individual 3D geometry.

4
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:12,540
The developers separated rough grain, tiny glints,

5
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:13,880
and broad highlights.

6
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:15,980
First, small patterns describe

7
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:17,720
which way the sand surface faces.

8
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:19,940
That direction is called a normal.

9
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:21,960
But in smaller textures used at a distance,

10
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:23,920
those directional differences blur together.

11
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:28,760
The team adjusted the distribution of directions to retain grain in smaller textures.

12
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:30,660
Tiny glints are added on top.

13
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:33,280
Apply sharp highlights to small grain,

14
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:35,060
and a still image can look convincing.

15
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:36,980
But when the camera moves,

16
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:39,680
bright points may flicker unstably.

17
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:42,680
Intended sparkle and unstable flickering are different.

18
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:46,100
The team changed how the glints are calculated.

19
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:49,580
They used a different relationship instead of the light–view halfway direction.

20
00:00:49,580 --> 00:00:52,180
It is the relationship between the surface and the view.

21
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:54,440
This adjusts the tiny lights revealed

22
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:55,820
as the camera moves.

23
00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:57,860
The presentation does not establish this

24
00:00:57,860 --> 00:00:59,440
as an exact physical law.

25
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:01,000
Near the edge of a sand dune,

26
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,740
when we see the surface obliquely,

27
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:05,160
the pattern can stretch and spread.

28
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:06,200
A mask identifies these regions

29
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:09,440
and reduces the glint effect there.

30
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:11,920
Instead of applying it strongly everywhere,

31
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:13,960
the problematic regions are handled separately.

32
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:17,120
Finally, broad light flows over the dunes.

33
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:19,720
This reflection reveals their large shapes.

34
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:22,040
Three treatments of light come together to complete the sand.
